1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,420
Have you ever been in a lift with the big cheese in your company?
你有没有和公司的大人物一起坐过电梯？

2
00:00:04,420 --> 00:00:07,230
It happened to me a couple of times.
这种事在我身上发生过几次。

3
00:00:07,230 --> 00:00:12,920
And did I take advantage of the situation to deliver my elevator pitch?
我有没有利用这个机会做电梯自我推销？

4
00:00:12,920 --> 00:00:14,590
Not a chance.
绝无可能。

5
00:00:14,590 --> 00:00:19,930
He was surrounded by people buttering him up all the way to the top floor!
他被一群人围着奉承，一直到顶楼！

6
00:00:19,930 --> 00:00:23,120
Lifts have an interesting history.
电梯有一段有趣的历史。

7
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:28,590
Today, the more important you are, the higher you live or work.
如今，你越重要，你居住或工作的地方就越高。

8
00:00:28,590 --> 00:00:33,480
Penthouses have fantastic views for boardrooms and living rooms.
顶层公寓为会议室和客厅提供了绝佳的视野。

9
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:36,650
But it hasn't always been that way.
但过去并非总是如此。

10
00:00:36,650 --> 00:00:43,260
Before the days of lifts, richer people would often prefer to live on the ground floor.
在电梯出现之前，富人通常更喜欢住在一楼。

11
00:00:43,260 --> 00:00:49,360
Poorer people lived on the upper floors – and they had to use the stairs.
穷人则住在更高的楼层——因此他们不得不使用楼梯。

12
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:57,730
In any case, whatever your pay grade, the confined space of a lift makes for an awkward encounter.
无论如何，无论你的薪资级别如何，电梯狭小的空间必然导致尴尬的偶遇。

13
00:00:57,730 --> 00:01:07,640
It's hard not to notice the uneasiness of a group of strangers in a confined space who have no time to develop any kind of bond.
很难注意不到一群陌生人在狭小空间中的不安，他们没有时间建立任何联系。

14
00:01:07,640 --> 00:01:13,060
But if marketing people have their way, that's all going to change.
但如果营销人员得逞，这一切都将改变。

15
00:01:13,060 --> 00:01:23,240
Jason Whale, sales manager at Elevators Ltd, says: "It's a very anxious experience the time you spend in a lift.
电梯有限公司的销售经理杰森·威尔（Jason Whale）说：“在电梯里度过时光是一种非常焦虑的体验。

16
00:01:23,240 --> 00:01:27,950
If you have things around you, you take away that awkwardness.
如果你周围有东西，你会消除那种尴尬。

17
00:01:27,950 --> 00:01:32,560
We all look at our phones sometimes or look down at the floor.
我们有时会看手机或低头看地板。

18
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:38,010
Well, surely it's better to look at advertisements on the walls…"
嗯，看墙上的广告肯定更好……”

19
00:01:38,010 --> 00:01:44,170
He sees a lot of potential in this box in which we spend a few minutes every day.
他看到了这个我们每天花几分钟待着的“盒子”的巨大潜力。

20
00:01:44,170 --> 00:01:57,330
Whale explains: "As technology becomes slimmer and cheaper, there are so many different ways to enhance a lift with light boxes, with moving images, with television screens!
威尔解释说：“随着技术变得更轻薄、更便宜，有很多不同的方式来增强电梯的功能，比如用灯箱、动态图像和电视屏幕！

21
00:01:57,330 --> 00:02:04,810
It becomes quite exciting for us, and hopefully a little bit more interesting for the people who use lifts."
这对我们来说非常令人兴奋，也希望电梯使用者能觉得更有趣一些。”

22
00:02:04,810 --> 00:02:08,370
Who knows what the lifts of the future will look like?
谁知道未来的电梯会是什么样子？

23
00:02:08,370 --> 00:02:12,540
Perhaps they will become the places where everybody wants to be.
也许它们会成为每个人都想去的地方。

24
00:02:12,540 --> 00:02:14,700
Time for a business meeting?
是时候开商务会议了吗？

25
00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:16,220
Ready to party?
准备好派对了？

26
00:02:16,220 --> 00:02:19,400
Come on everybody, let's get into the lift!
来吧，大家，我们进电梯吧！
